avily on offchain IP stewardship, portal availability, and product execution by Orange Cap Games.","source_ids":["moonbirds-proof","moonbirds-current","moonbirds-ocg"]},"forensic_analysis":{"version":"forensic-analysis-v1","outcome":{"label":"middling","scope":"Moonbirds collection and current IP stewardship, not historical floor-price performance","summary":"Moonbirds retains a live legacy portal and recognizable IP under Orange Cap Games, but current demand, holder participation, product adoption, and value transfer to NFTs remain unproven.","confidence":"high","as_of":"2026-07-27","source_refs":["moonbirds-current","moonbirds-ocg"]},"why":{"summary":"Observed: the collection, nesting history, portal, and IP family survived an ownership transition. Inference: recognizable identity and preserved utility prevented a terminal outcome, while the absence of shipped replacement products or current demand evidence prevents a thriving classification.","basis":"current operator and legacy-product evidence; demand conclusion is bounded analyst inference","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["moonbirds-proof","moonbirds-current","moonbirds-ocg"]},"strategic_choices":[{"decision":"Tie early community benefits to time-based nesting.","intended_mechanism":"Reward long-duration participation rather than ownership alone.","consequence":"Nesting created a differentiated loyalty mechanic, but also made legacy utility dependent on maintained operator infrastructure.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["moonbirds-proof"]},{"decision":"Preserve a legacy portal during the ownership transition.","intended_mechanism":"Avoid breaking existing holder access before replacement products are available.","consequence":"The portal reduces transition damage but does not prove new user acquisition or renewed collection demand.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["moonbirds-current"]},{"decision":"Consolidate Moonbirds, Mythics, and Oddities under Orange Cap Games.","intended_mechanism":"Place the