n.","intended_mechanism":"Reach collectors who did not want to manage crypto wallets directly.","consequence":"Nifty differentiated on access, while becoming strategically and operationally dependent on Gemini.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["nifty-acquisition","nifty-s1"]},{"decision":"Pair curated drops with studio production and a secondary marketplace.","intended_mechanism":"Control creator onboarding, launch quality, and ongoing trading in one venue.","consequence":"The full-service model created a recognizable platform but also required continuing curation, production, custody, and marketplace operations.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["nifty-s1"]},{"decision":"Wind down rather than maintain or separate the marketplace.","intended_mechanism":"Concentrate Gemini resources on its super-app strategy.","consequence":"Marketplace and studio operations ended; withdrawal support reduced custody harm but did not preserve the business.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["nifty-closure","nifty-8k"]}],"counterfactual":{"summary":"An independent sale, spinout, or lower-cost creator platform might have preserved Nifty''s brand and marketplace, but the reviewed sources do not show that Gemini pursued one or that it would have been commercially viable.","limits":"No platform-level revenue, cost, bid-depth, buyer-retention, or sale-process data are disclosed.","confidence":"low","source_refs":["nifty-risk","nifty-closure","nifty-8k"]},"watch":[{"signal":"Completion of remaining withdrawals and continued Gemini Wallet support for former Nifty assets.","implication":"Orderly asset access limits customer harm but does not change the terminal marketplace classification.","source_refs":["nifty-closure"]},{"signal":"A disclosed acquisition or relaunch of the Nifty Gateway brand, creator tooling, or marketplace.","implication":"A functioning successor could justify a recovery case scoped to that new operator.","source_refs":["nifty-closure","nifty-8k"]}],"unknowns":["What were Nifty Gateway''s final revenue, costs, active buyers, and trading liquidity?","Did Gemini solicit a sale, spinout, or licensing transaction before closure?","Were all custodial assets withdrawn or migrated successfully?","What continuing rights or obligations remain for artists whose drops were produced by Nifty Gateway?"],"review":{"status":"current","last_reviewed_at":"2026-07-29","next_review_at":"2027-02-23","reviewer":"chaindump-research-desk"}}},"sources":[{"id":"nifty-acquisition","title":"Gemini Expands Into NFTs With Nifty Gateway","url":"https://www.gemini.com/blog/gemini-expands-into-non-fungible-tokens-nfts-with-nifty-gateway-tm","checked_at":"2026-07-29"},{"id":"nifty-s1","title":"Gemini Space Station S-1 — Nifty Gateway Studio description","url":"https://investors.gemini.com/static-files/387885d9-75c0-4524-95b4-d550890aad3e","checked_at":"2026-07-29"},{"id":"nifty-risk","title":"Gemini Q3 2025 Form 10-Q — NFT business risk","url":"https://investors.gemini.com/static-files/0385bebc-c005-47c3-9704-a71ef00ec224","checked_at":"2026-07-29"},{"id":"nifty-closure","title":"Announcing Nifty Gateway''s Closure","url":"https://www.gemini.com/es/blog/announcing-nifty-gateways-closure","checked_at":"2026-07-29"},{"id":"nifty-8k","title":"Gemini March 2026 Form 8-K — Nifty Gateway wound down","url":"https://investors.gemini.com/static-files/9930b4f9-4e24-4f9a-8b7b-fb5066554c86","checked_at":"2026-07-29"},{"id":"nifty-help","title":"Nifty Gateway Support Center","url":"https://help.niftygateway.com/hc/en-us","checked_at":"2026-07-29","access_state":"bot_blocked","verification_note":"Automated GET returned HTTP 403 on 2026-07-29; retained as prior-reviewed support evidence, not independent current-state verification."}]},{"slug":"nouns-dao","status":"thriving","profile":{"token_model":{"finding":"The NFT itself is the governance instrument: one Noun is auctioned every 24 hours, auction proceeds enter the DAO treasury, and Noun owners or delegates vote on proposals. No separate fungible token is required by this model.","boundary":"Treasury funding and governance rights are observable; treasury performance, voter quality, and NFT investment returns are not inferred.","source_ids":["nouns-token","nouns-auction","nouns-governance"]},"chain_dependence":{"finding":"Ethereum contracts coordinate issuance, auctions, ownership, treasury funding, and governance. Community projects funded by the DAO can exist offchain, but the core capital-and-control loop depends on Ethereum.","source_ids":["nouns-token","nouns-auction","nouns-governance"]},"forensic_analysis":{"version":"forensic-analysis-v1","outcome":{"label":"thriving","scope":"Nouns issuance and governance protocol, not secondary-market returns or proposal quality","summary":"Nouns continues its protocol-defined daily auction and holder-governance loop. The label reflects live issuance and governance, not price performance.","confidence":"high","as_of":"2026-07-28","source_refs":["nouns-auction","nouns-governance"]},"why":{"summary":"Observed: one new Noun is auctioned every 24 hours, proceeds fund a holder-controlled treasury, and proposals are voted by holders and delegates. Inference: recurring primary issuance finances continuing coordination without relying only on royalties; open-ended supply and governance effectiveness remain tradeoffs.","basis":"onchain and operator mechanism evidence; durability interpretation is analyst synthesis","confidence":"high","source_refs":["nouns-token","nouns-auction","nouns-governance"]},"strategic_choices":[{"decision":"Issue one Noun through an auction every 24 hours with no fixed terminal supply.","intended_mechanism":"Create a perpetual cadence for membership and treasury funding.","consequence":"The DAO gains recurring primary capital and onboarding, while holders accept continuing supply expansion.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["nouns-auction"]},{"decision":"Send auction proceeds to a treasury controlled by Noun owners.","intended_mechanism":"Convert primary sales into collectively governed capital.","consequence":"NFT ownership carries budget authority, but treasury deployment quality depends on proposal and voter governance.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["nouns-auction","nouns-governance"]},{"decision":"Use the NFT as the voting unit and allow delegation.","intended_mechanism":"Align membership, capital formation, and governance in one asset.","consequence":"The model avoids a separate governance token while concentrating formal influence with Noun ownership and delegates.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["nouns-governance"]}],"counterfactual":{"summary":"A fixed-supply launch could have reduced dilution and simplified scarcity, but it would have removed the protocol''s recurring auction funding and continuous membership mechanism. The evidence does not establish which model would produce better governance or holder returns.","limits":"No controlled comparison of treasury efficiency, voter participation, or holder outcomes is available.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["nouns-auction","nouns-governance"]},"watch":[{"signal":"Daily auctions continue to clear and fund the treasury.","implication":"Persistent issuance demand supports the core operating loop; extended auction failure would weaken it.","source_refs":["nouns-auction"]},{"signal":"Proposal participation, delegation concentration, and treasury deployment outcomes.","implication":"These determine whether formal governance produces useful coordination rather than only live contracts.","source_refs":["nouns-governance"]},{"signal":"Any change to auction cadence, voting rights, or treasury control.","implication":"A mechanism change would alter the core value-capture and governance thesis.","source_refs":["nouns-auction","nouns-governance"]}],"unknowns":["How concentrated are current voting power and delegated votes?","What share of treasury spending produces durable public goods or measurable adoption?","How many a