ucts; market-demand causality withheld","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["wow-home","wow-about","wow-community","wow-patio"]},"strategic_choices":[{"decision":"Anchor the brand in a fixed 10,000-avatar collection centered on representation.","intended_mechanism":"Create a recognizable identity and community underserved by earlier PFP brands.","consequence":"World of Women gained a durable cultural position, while cultural recognition alone could not guarantee operating or market success.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["wow-home","wow-about"]},{"decision":"Expand through a separate 22,222-avatar Galaxy series.","intended_mechanism":"Broaden participation and extend the IP family.","consequence":"The brand reached more holders while increasing supply, segmentation, and cross-collection coordination risk.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["wow-home"]},{"decision":"Build Patio for profiles, discovery, customization, and community events.","intended_mechanism":"Give ownership a maintained social-product layer.","consequence":"Patio creates utility beyond display, while adding operator hosting, adoption, and moderation dependencies.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["wow-patio","wow-community"]},{"decision":"Rebuild the team and frame 2026 as a new operating era.","intended_mechanism":"Reset execution and restore delivery capacity.","consequence":"The rebuild demonstrates adaptation, but also makes future delivery and trust recovery the decisive tests.","confidence":"high","source_refs":["wow-about"]}],"counterfactual":{"summary":"Remaining a single static collection would have protected focus but left the project with less social utility. Expansion and Patio can deepen community use, while additional supply and product overhead may dilute attention if the rebuilt team cannot sustain delivery.","limits":"Patio cohorts, event retention, collection overlap, revenue, and liquidity are unavailable.","confidence":"medium","source_refs":["wow-home","wow-about","wow